Ofsted\'92s cr\'e8che exemption requires several conditions, including a maximum of four hours daily for under-eights, parents remaining close enough to summon immediately, and short-term convenience without commitment. Its guidance specifically says childcare supporting work or training over several weeks is not exempt under that provision. **A parent remaining in the co-working room does not, by itself, establish an exemption.** [Ofsted registration exemptions](https://www.gov.uk/guidance/childcare-registration-exemptions)\
\
Your proposed service should therefore be mapped explicitly to its registration requirements. A registered childcare operation could be part of the concept; its staffing, space and pricing would need to support that promise.\
