**Three particularly useful insights emerge.**\
\
**The nursery\'92s 281 m\'b2 is children\'92s accommodation, rather than its whole footprint.** The schedule allocates 49 m\'b2 to babies, 101 m\'b2 to two-to-threes and 131 m\'b2 to three-to-fives, with a proposed capacity of **111 children**. Reception, kitchen, staff facilities, toilets and circulation sit beyond those children\'92s-room areas. We therefore cannot compare 281 m\'b2 with the whole club\'92s 2,010 m\'b2 to calculate a meaningful nursery/club percentage.\
\
That 111 is also a **design annotation**, not confirmation of registered capacity. These nursery drawings are marked draft, with revisions through July 2023.\
\
**The nursery building contains club support functions.** There is a **52 m\'b2 club staffroom/office** downstairs and a **33 m\'b2 club store** upstairs: approximately **915 sq ft supporting the club within the nursery premises**. For our financial model, allocating every cost of that building to childcare would misrepresent the functions shown. We would need explicit allocations for shared premises and support costs.\
\
**They provide substantial childcare accommodation twice.** The full-day nursery operates separately from the club\'92s **207 m\'b2 kids-club suite**, which includes a baby room, kids\'92 room, studio and reception. For your concept, this reinforces the need to budget separately for nursery places and flexible member childcare.\
\
The hospitality annotations are useful too: a **190 m\'b2 restaurant**, **86 m\'b2 living-room caf\'e9**, **54 m\'b2 grab-and-go/bar**, plus a main kitchen and upstairs finishing kitchen.\
\
For property comparisons, we now have a documented **21,635 sq ft internal NIA benchmark for the proposed club**. We still need to reconcile that with the earlier 30,000 sq ft marketing headline and establish the nursery\'92s full building area. The drawings also do not validate our smaller concept\'92s preliminary 8,000\'9612,000 sq ft allowance.\
